{
  "id": "b2-e05-learning-in-different-ways",
  "level": "B2",
  "version": 1,
  "topic": "Learning in different ways",
  "parts": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "title": "Interview",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p1-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "Good evening. First of all, we'd like to know something about you.",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e05-learning-in-different-ways/p1-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4400
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q1",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "text": "Candidate A, what are you studying or what do you do for a living?",
          "durationSec": 25,
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e05-learning-in-different-ways/p1-q1.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4400
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q2",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "text": "Candidate B, what is the most interesting thing you have learnt recently?",
          "durationSec": 25,
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e05-learning-in-different-ways/p1-q2.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4900
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q3",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "text": "Candidate A, do you find it easy to learn new things?",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e05-learning-in-different-ways/p1-q3.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4000
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q4",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "text": "Candidate B, how do you prefer to study, alone or with other people?",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e05-learning-in-different-ways/p1-q4.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5200
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "title": "Long turn",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p2-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "In this part of the test, I'm going to give each of you two photographs. I'd like you to talk about them on your own for about a minute, and also to answer a question about your partner's photographs.",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e05-learning-in-different-ways/p2-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 13000
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-a",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 60,
          "assets": [
            "b2-e05-a1",
            "b2-e05-a2"
          ],
          "text": "Candidate A, your photographs show people learning in different ways. Compare the photographs, and say what the advantages and disadvantages of learning in these ways might be.",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e05-learning-in-different-ways/p2-a.mp3",
          "audioMs": 12100
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-a-follow",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "text": "Candidate B, which way of learning would you prefer? Why?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e05-learning-in-different-ways/p2-a-follow.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4500
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-b",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 60,
          "assets": [
            "b2-e05-b1",
            "b2-e05-b2"
          ],
          "text": "Candidate B, your photographs show people learning something. Compare the photographs, and say how interested the people might be.",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e05-learning-in-different-ways/p2-b.mp3",
          "audioMs": 8800
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-b-follow",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "text": "Candidate A, do you think it is easier to learn when you are younger? Why?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e05-learning-in-different-ways/p2-b-follow.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5100
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "title": "Collaborative task",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p3-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "Now I'd like you to talk about something together for about two minutes. Here are some things that can help students learn, and a question for you to discuss.",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e05-learning-in-different-ways/p3-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 9700
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-discuss",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 120,
          "diagram": "b2-e05-learning-in-different-ways",
          "text": "Talk to each other about this question: How might these things help students learn better?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e05-learning-in-different-ways/p3-discuss.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5900
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-decide",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 60,
          "diagram": "b2-e05-learning-in-different-ways",
          "text": "Now you have about a minute to decide together. Which would be the most useful for students?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e05-learning-in-different-ways/p3-decide.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5900
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "title": "Discussion",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p4-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "Now I'd like to ask you some more questions about education and learning.",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e05-learning-in-different-ways/p4-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5500
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q1",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 50,
          "text": "Some people say that school does not prepare young people for real life. How far do you agree?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e05-learning-in-different-ways/p4-q1.mp3",
          "audioMs": 6300
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q2",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate A, what is the best teacher you have ever had, and why?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e05-learning-in-different-ways/p4-q2.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4800
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q3",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate B, do you think exams are a good way to measure what students know?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e05-learning-in-different-ways/p4-q3.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5600
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q4",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 50,
          "text": "Should students be able to choose all their subjects at school?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e05-learning-in-different-ways/p4-q4.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4100
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q5",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate A, how important is it to continue studying after you finish school?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e05-learning-in-different-ways/p4-q5.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5700
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
